      <Comment source="AU4FS-4, SRI, caspi">|FRAME: CPD-8654 Betanin| is a red glycosidic compound that gives beet roots their characteristic color. The concentration of betanin in red beet can reach 300-600 mg/kg. The aglycone, obtained by hydrolyzing away the glucose molecule, is |FRAME: CPD-8653|. Betanin absorbs well in the gut and acts as an antioxidant.</Comment>
